[[Lord]] '''Janu''' was a [[warlord]] in the [[Neo-Imperial forces|remnants]] of the [[Galactic Empire]] who carried out [[Pillage of hyperspace routes|hit-and-run attacks]] around [[9 ABY]]. He held the [[Military rank|rank]] of [[commander]] and were a part of the [[Shadow Council (Imperial Remnants)|Shadow Council]], a group of [[Imperial officer]]s who secretly operated in concert against the [[New Republic]]. Around that [[Standard year|year]], the commander attended a meeting of the council via [[hologram]], in the process briefly arguing with [[Captain]] [[Gilad Pellaeon]]. Janu later sat in the stands of an arena, between the [[youngling]] [[Din Grogu]], who had been [[prison|imprisoned]] in a cage, and the [[Iktotchi]] [[Hogsbreth]].

==Biography==
{{Quote|Commander, your hit-and-run operations are gaining too much notice. If we are perceived as anything other than a group of unorganized remnant warlords, the New Republic will increase their efforts to hunt us down.|Captain Gilad Pellaeon, to Janu|audio=Pellaeon-MuchNotice.flac|<ref name="Chapter23" />}}
[[Lord]] Janu<ref name="Getty">{{Getty|url=thewaltdisneystudios/allaccess/#!asset/hc968sf4xx57p8snxm8pb93s|text=THND-013615 R|author=[[The Walt Disney Company|The Walt Disney Studios]]|date=2026-03-24}}</ref> was a [[warlord]] of one of the [[Neo-Imperial forces|remnants]] of the [[Galactic Empire]] was active<ref name="Chapter23" /> around [[9 ABY]].<ref name="Date">{{MandoDate|23}}</ref> Holding the [[Military rank|rank]] of [[commander]], Janu was a part of the [[Shadow Council (Imperial Remnants)|Shadow Council]], a group of [[Imperial officer]]s who secretly cooperated during the [[New Republic Era|era]] of the [[New Republic]] and each furthered Imperial interests within a specific [[sector]] of [[the galaxy]]. Janu specifically carried out [[Pillage of hyperspace routes|hit-and-run attacks]] on [[hyperspace route]]s with the aim of acquiring valuable loot.<ref name="Chapter23" />

[[File:MandoShadowCouncil.png|thumb|left|300px|Lord Janu was a member of the Shadow Council.]]
At one point around 9 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]],<ref name="Date" /> Janu was attending via [[hologram]] a meeting of the Shadow Council. During the meeting, he expressed his disagreement with [[Captain]] [[Gilad Pellaeon]], who urged the members of the council to be discreet about revealing to the New Republic the true strength of their forces. In response to the Janu's remark, Pellaeon noted that the attacks the former was carrying was attracting too much notice.<ref name="Chapter23" />

Later during the meeting, Janu attentively observed the arguing between Pellaeon, [[Commandant]] [[Brendol Hux]], and [[Moff]] [[Gideon]] over the allotment of Imperial resources. Janu and two others also agreed with Gideon's claim that, unlike the Imperial factions represented by Pellaeon and Hux, the other members of the Shadow Council restricted their undertakings to reporting on the events that transpired within their respective sectors. When Gideon subsequently described a plan to [[Liberation of Mandalore|exterminate]] the remaining members of the [[Mandalorian]] [[Mandalorian warrior|warrior]] culture and shouted a [[Long live the Empire|hail]] to the continued longevity of the Empire, the other Imperial [[officer]]s present in the meeting echoed the hail.<ref name="Chapter23" />

[[File:Grogu and Janu and Hogsbreath.jpg|thumb|right|220px|Lord Janu watches an arena intently]]
Sometime after the [[death]] of fellow council member [[Moff]] Gideon during the [[Liberation of Mandalore]], Lord Janu sat in the stands of an arena beside a caged Din Grogu, the adoptive son of [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]], who had been tasked by New Republic [[Colonel]] [[Ward]] with hunting down [[Hutt]] gangsters, and Imperial Remnant war criminals like the Janu himself.<ref name="Empire" /> To his other side sat the Iktotchi Hogsbreth.<ref name=Getty />

==Personality and traits==
Janu was a bald, light-skinned [[human]]<ref name="Chapter23" /> [[Gender|male]].<ref name="Chapter23SB" />

==Equipment==
Janu wore an unadorned [[Color|black]] [[Imperial officer's uniform]] with a [[belt]] and a pair of black [[glove]]s and [[boot]]s whilst attending a Shadow Council meeting via hologram.<ref name="Chapter23" /> He later wore a red shirt beneath a grey suit jacket, when sitting in an arena's stands.<ref name="Empire" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Warlord-1-Mando.png|thumb|right|220px|Lord Janu's appearance in "Chapter 23: The Spies"]]
{{Quote|You'll like his character name when you hear it.|Jon Favreau|<ref name="Empire" />}}
Lord Janu, portrayed by [[Jonny Coyne]], appeared in hologram form in "[[Chapter 23: The Spies]],"<ref name="Chapter23" /> the seventh episode of the [[Disney+]] television show ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]''{{'s}} [[The Mandalorian Season Three|third season]], though was only referred as "Commander" and was credited as one of a number of "Warlords". The episode aired on [[April 12]], [[2023]].<ref name="Companion">{{InsiderCite|222|Star Wars: The Mandalorian Season Three Companion|''Star Wars: The Mandalorian'' Season Three Companion}}</ref> Janu was confirmed to be returning for the [[May 22]], [[2026]] live-action film, ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian and Grogu]]'', in the [[May]] [[2026]] issue of [[Wikipedia:Empire (magazine)|''Empire'']] magazine, with director and co-writer [[Jon Favreau]] teasing that fans would like the warlord's name when they heard it.<ref name="Empire" /> Janu's name was revealed by the caption of image from the magazine issue when it was posted on [[Wikipedia:Getty Images|Getty Images]] on [[March 24]], 2026.<ref name="Getty" />

